{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts security deposit limit, interest and return","requirement":"A landlord may not hold a security deposit above one month's rent, must keep it in a separate interest-bearing account, pay 5% yearly interest, and return it with an itemized damage list within 30 days of move-out.","key_value":"1 month's rent; 5% interest per year; 30-day return","coverage_conditions":"Applies to residential real property leases; the text states no building-age, unit-count or owner limit.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Residential real property leases"},"exemptions":"No deduction for reasonable wear and tear or for damage listed in the pre-tenancy condition statement; successor liability does not apply to a city or town acquiring title under chapter 60 or to certain mortgagees.","penalty":"A lessor who fails to hold, account for or return the deposit forfeits the right to retain any portion and is liable for three times the deposit plus 5% interest, court costs and reasonable attorney's fees.","effective_date":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(4) The lessor shall, within thirty days after the termination of occupancy under a tenancy-at-will or the end of the tenancy as specified in a valid written lease agreement, return to the tenant the security deposit or any balance thereof","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts cap on advance payments at start of tenancy","requirement":"No landlord or agent may require a tenant to pay before tenancy more than first month's rent, last month's rent, a one-month security deposit and key/lock cost; a fee in lieu of deposit is capped at one month's rent.","key_value":"first + last month's rent + 1 month deposit + key/lock cost","coverage_conditions":"All residential real property leases in Massachusetts; no building-age, unit-count or owner limit stated. A fee-in-lieu-of-deposit option requires executive office (HLC) regulations.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Residential real property leases"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"A lease provision conflicting with this section, or a demand for a waiver of it, forfeits the landlord's right to retain any security deposit.","effective_date":"2025-08-01","citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(b) At or prior to the commencement of any tenancy, no lessor or agent of the lessor may require a tenant or prospective tenant to pay, to the lessor or to an agent of the lessor, any amount in excess of the following:  (i) rent for the first full month of occupancy;  and, (ii) rent for the last full month of occupancy calculated at the same rate as the first month;  and, (iii) a security deposit equal to the first month's rent","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
